              {
                "text": "**Analyzing the Training Data**\n\nI'm currently focused on the training data provided, trying to decipher the relationship between inputs and outputs. I'm noting specific patterns, like how the value '3' in the input correlates with its representation in the output. I'm also examining the lengths and positions of various numerical sequences. I'm building up the mental model through these observations.\n\n\n**Investigating Shifting Patterns**\n\nI'm starting to see a pattern! It seems like the primary operation involves shifting numerical sequences to the left. I've found multiple instances across different training sets where the position of a number is reduced by one. However, the exact rule still eludes me. I will keep exploring how shifting interacts with length and the background value.\n\n\n**Uncovering Sequence Transformation**\n\nI've made a breakthrough! It appears the key operation is a leftward shift of segments within the input sequence. Each segment's starting column is reduced by one, and if the shifted segment would extend beyond the start of the output (column 0), it is truncated. This explains the reduction of segment lengths as well. I'm verifying this concept with other test inputs.\n\n\n**Confirming Grid Shift**\n\nI've got it! It's not just a segment, but the whole grid shifting left by one cell. Zeros become fives as the background. I'm verifying this across Train 1, 2, and 3 now, confirming the model with each new line. The pattern of shifting and background replacement is consistent!\n\n\n",
